# Build output. `/build*/` and not `/build/` plus `/build-*/`: the second pattern needs a hyphen, so
# `build2/` matched neither and 1432 files of generated .vcxproj, CMake cache and MSBuild logs -- 3.9 MB,
# every one of them holding this machine's absolute paths -- were committed for months. Every `git
# status` opened with dozens of them, which is how the ones that mattered stopped being read.
/build*/
/out/
out.ll

# Native build artifacts
*.exe
*.obj
*.o
*.a
*.lib
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.exp

# CMake
CMakeUserPresets.json

# vcpkg (dependencies live outside the repo)
/vcpkg_installed/

# Editor / IDE
.vs/
.vscode/
*.user

dist/
installer/.cache/

# kernel build artifacts
kernel/*.o
kernel/*.ll
kernel/kernel.elf
kernel/*.dump
kernel/qemu.log

# branding intermediates
branding/preview-*.png
branding/_render.html
docs/reference/_reference.html

# LLVM IR emitted next to a sample when polc is run on it by hand
tests/samples/*.ll

# The bare-metal port projects build IN PLACE, because `polaron build` builds a project where the
# project is -- so the images the AArch64 and i686 boot tests produce land next to their manifests.
tests/*/build-output/

# stray IR dumps at the repo root (polc -o na.ll etc.)
/*.ll

# Working documents, deliberately not published (see docs/reference/ for the public reference).
# Removed once already; re-added by a careless `git add -A docs`, so the pattern is written down.
docs/superpowers/
docs/IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS.md
docs/POLARON_state.md
docs/POLARON_specification.md
docs/POLARON_keywords.md
NIGHT_PROGRESS*.md
MUDANCAS.md
PENDENTE.md
polaron_analise.md
ctest_*.log*
# A scratch file keeps its .tmp and gains an extension: `forge_todo_test.tmp.pol`. `*.tmp` alone does
# not match that, so two of them from a Forge run sat committed in the repository root -- five lines of
# nothing, on the front page of a public repository.
*.tmp
*.tmp.*
